        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"BenjaminTodd\"]\n\nDeadline&#39;s Pandemonium Key reads:\n<blockquote>The first time an environment target enters play each turn, play the top card of the villian deck.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\ndoes this apply when any given envirnomental target enters play or any given type of environmental target?&nbsp; For instance, if The Final Wasteland, if an Amphibious Chupacabra is turned over in two different turns, is that considered one or two targets and therefor two villian card plays?&nbsp;The &quot;The first time&quot; phrasing is confusing me, but I read it as each one would trigger the villian card play.Thanks,Ben\n\n[/quote]\n\nUsually that wording means that if circumstances in that turn trigger the environment playing another card that happens to be a target - you do not trigger the effect again.\n\nAnd if the Amphibs came out during different turns it would mean that two villain cards would be played.\n\n&nbsp;\n",
